  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689624",
      "title": "Using \"tick()\"",
      "lectureOrder": 67,
      "videoOrder": 59,
      "sourceHash": "9e43d1818252a5bed813e98f3ddb6d893aef742847b537901796c0f46925760c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.01,
          "end": 6.66,
          "en": "Now tick is a bit more complex to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 14.64,
          "en": "Hence here in Apps world, I'll try to provide a relatively simple example which admittedly is taken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 14.64,
          "end": 20.49,
          "en": "from the official docs because there we have a good example and it's so rare that you need to use tick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 20.49,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "So that's really important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "Using tick just as before and after update, you won't do it that often, which is why there aren't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "that many great examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 30.97,
          "en": "So let's use it here in App Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.99,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "Let's first of all import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "So let's import tick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.82,
          "end": 37.66,
          "en": "From.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.06,
          "end": 44.98,
          "en": "Svelte like this with that imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.31,
          "end": 46.93,
          "en": "Let's see how we can use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.05,
          "end": 51.91,
          "en": "Let's add a text area here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.45,
          "end": 57.87,
          "en": "Doesn't need a name, doesn't add an ID, doesn't need columns, but I want to have rows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 57.88,
          "end": 59.11,
          "en": "Let's say five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "And now in their.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.74,
          "end": 68.51,
          "en": "When I output some text, so I'll bind to text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.61,
          "en": "And I'll set text as a variable up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 74.51,
          "en": "Let text equals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "This is some dummy text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "Now my idea is that we can select this text and when we hit the tab button, then this is transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 84.9,
          "en": "to uppercase text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 87.32,
          "en": "So this text should be output in the text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 89.35,
          "en": "Let's quickly check whether that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "Yes, here it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 93.97,
          "en": "And now I want to be able to select some text and hit tab.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.99000000000001,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "Right now, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "We just unselect it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.78,
          "en": "But in the future I don't want to unselect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "Instead, the selected text should be transformed to uppercase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.55,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "It's just an example, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "So for this, let's add a new function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.7,
          "end": 110.87,
          "en": "Transform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.65,
          "end": 113.3,
          "en": "You can name it whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "And we'll get an event here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 121.83,
          "en": "And this function should fire whenever we press a key on the keyboard, which is done with the key down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 123.89,
          "en": "event, that's a default Dom event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 127.65,
          "en": "And there I want to trigger well, transform as I just said.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.51,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "So transform will be triggered now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.22,
          "end": 132.95,
          "en": "Of course, we could be pressing any key when we type text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.95,
          "end": 135.11,
          "en": "We're pressing keys all the all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.11,
          "end": 139.34,
          "en": "So first of all, I want to check which key was pressed and if event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.54,
          "end": 142.91,
          "en": "Which is not equal to nine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.94,
          "end": 145.31,
          "en": "I therefore want to return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.32,
          "end": 148.99,
          "en": "With which we find out which key was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.99,
          "end": 152.32999999999998,
          "en": "And the key code for the tab key is nine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.35,
          "end": 154.24,
          "en": "So if it's not nine, then we return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.24,
          "end": 157.72,
          "en": "We only proceed if it is nine, which means the tab key was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.29,
          "end": 164.59,
          "en": "Then I'll prevent the default because the default would be that we now leave this input that we navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.59,
          "end": 168.52,
          "en": "to the next selectable field or element on our page and don't want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.52,
          "end": 174.7,
          "en": "So then I prevent the default and now I want to find out which part we selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.97,
          "end": 182.86,
          "en": "For this we can extract information like the selection start from event, which has a selection start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.86,
          "end": 183.49,
          "en": "field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.52,
          "end": 186.85,
          "en": "The event object here will have that selection start event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.89,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "I also, of course, want to get the selection end, which I also get from event selection end like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 194.97,
          "en": "this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 199.03,
          "end": 203.75,
          "en": "And last but not least, the value can also be retrieved from event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.48,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "Target value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "And this, by the way, here is also event target.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "So event target selection, start event, target selection, end event, target value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 214.89,
          "en": "These are the three pieces I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 214.92000000000002,
          "end": 222.78,
          "en": "Now with this extracted, let's set text, which is this variable we output in our text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 222.81,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "Let's set text equal to value slice zero two Selection Start to get the text up to the place we selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.63,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "plus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 234.17000000000002,
          "end": 245.15,
          "en": "Value slice selection, start selection end, which is the text we did select to uppercase plus value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 245.15,
          "end": 249.11,
          "en": "slice and now selection end to the end of the string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 249.11,
          "end": 255.44,
          "en": "So I'm simply generating a new string here which simply consists of the part we didn't select in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 255.44,
          "end": 260.54,
          "en": "of the selection and after the selection and in between our selection transform to uppercase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 260.54,
          "end": 261.71,
          "en": "This is our new text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 261.71,
          "end": 269.66,
          "en": "And since text is bound to the text area, this automatically is added back in there with this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 269.69,
          "end": 272.9,
          "en": "If we save this, we should be able to select this hit tab.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 272.9,
          "end": 276.29,
          "en": "And indeed it was transformed pretty good, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 277.35,
          "end": 283.05,
          "en": "But you might note that when I hit Tab, we lose the selection and the cursor jumps to the end because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 283.05,
          "end": 289.11,
          "en": "the Dom is updated and the cursor position in our selection simply is not something that would be saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 289.68,
          "end": 293.1,
          "en": "If we want to save this, we have to do it on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 293.1,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "And actually we do know which part was selected, so we just need to set the selection again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 297.57,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "Right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 300.9,
          "en": "So we can go back here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 301.73,
          "end": 310.13,
          "en": "And simply set event target selection start equal to the selection start we had here and do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 310.13,
          "end": 310.88,
          "en": "for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 311.91,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "The so selection end is set equal to selection end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 315.18,
          "end": 315.57,
          "en": "Right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 315.57,
          "end": 320.85,
          "en": "Because we're getting the selected text, we're updating it, this updates the Dom and thereafter we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 320.85,
          "end": 327.06,
          "en": "take the target of the event, which is our text area and set the selection again if we now save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 328.64,
          "end": 329.57,
          "en": "Here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 329.66,
          "end": 332.69,
          "en": "I hit tab and it doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 333.11,
          "end": 335.62,
          "en": "Now, the problem is what I described before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 335.63,
          "end": 341.6,
          "en": "When you change something like this text variable, which actually will lead to a Dom update because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 341.6,
          "end": 347.9,
          "en": "we're using it here in the Dom and Svelte finds out that when text changes, the value here changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 347.9,
          "end": 351.08,
          "en": "and it needs to update the Dom when this happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 351.38,
          "end": 355.34000000000003,
          "en": "Svelte does not pause code execution and instantly do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 355.37,
          "end": 357.35,
          "en": "Instead it schedules this task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 357.35,
          "end": 358.04,
          "en": "It now knows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 358.04,
          "end": 358.4,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 358.4,
          "end": 358.67,
          "en": "Yeah.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 358.67,
          "end": 365.63,
          "en": "I need to set that text here in the text area and I'll do this in the next micro task in the next schedule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 365.63,
          "end": 372.38,
          "en": "Dom update task, which of course will happen super fast so that we don't really see that pause in between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 372.38,
          "end": 374.51,
          "en": "this command and the real update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 374.51,
          "end": 380.48,
          "en": "But it still is there and hence it continues executing the code and it runs this code before the Dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 380.48,
          "end": 382.13,
          "en": "update was actually done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 383.87,
          "end": 387.44,
          "en": "Now, of course you could say, okay, so we have to put this in after update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 387.44,
          "end": 390.56,
          "en": "The problem just is we're in the middle of a function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 390.56,
          "end": 391.94,
          "en": "We can't add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 392.73,
          "end": 397.05,
          "en": "After update here and schedule our code to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 397.08,
          "end": 398.4,
          "en": "We can actually try that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 398.4,
          "end": 405.65999999999997,
          "en": "Let's import after update before we use tick and then let's use after update here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 406.51,
          "end": 407.92,
          "en": "Define our function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 407.92,
          "end": 411.55,
          "en": "Take that code and run it inside this after update function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 413.17,
          "end": 414.25,
          "en": "Just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 424.5,
          "end": 425.64,
          "en": "If we do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 427.56,
          "end": 428.82,
          "en": "Let's select this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 429.18,
          "end": 435.57,
          "en": "Now we even get an error function called outside of component initialization because you have to call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 435.6,
          "end": 443.31,
          "en": "on Mount Ondestroy before update and after update always outside of any function handlers directly inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 443.31,
          "end": 444.36,
          "en": "of these script tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 444.36,
          "end": 448.74,
          "en": "So the only valid place where you can register your after update handler is here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 448.86,
          "end": 454.23,
          "en": "The problem just is here you don't have access to event target selection, start and selection end because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 454.23,
          "end": 456.9,
          "en": "that is part of this transform function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 457.35,
          "end": 463.35,
          "en": "So after update is simply not the solution, but there is a possible way of getting this to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 463.71,
          "end": 467.07,
          "en": "All you have to do is use tick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 467.81,
          "end": 470.15,
          "en": "Tick actually returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 470.15,
          "end": 475.4,
          "en": "And when this promise is resolved, the next micro task will have been completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 475.61,
          "end": 478.04,
          "en": "So here we can add then and now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 478.04,
          "end": 485.03,
          "en": "In this then function, we pass a function which will therefore execute after the scheduled tasks have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 485.03,
          "end": 485.93,
          "en": "been done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 485.93,
          "end": 490.28,
          "en": "And this is now the place where we can safely execute this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 490.28,
          "end": 493.37,
          "en": "So here, this will not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 493.55,
          "end": 495.02,
          "en": "This code down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 495.29,
          "end": 498.62,
          "en": "This code in here, however, will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 499.89,
          "end": 502.23,
          "en": "So I'll comment this out here and now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
